  "articleBody": "Building a tiny home might seem like just a smaller version of building a regular house, but trust me, it's a whole different ballgame. It's not about scaling down; it's about building smarter and more intentionally. Zen Tiny Homes has been doing this for over a decade, so we've got this down.\n\nOne big difference is the focus on hyper-efficiency. Every single square foot needs to be multi-functional and optimized. You can't afford wasted space, so structural elements often double as storage or seating. Then there’s the sheer precision required. Small tolerances mean everything has to fit perfectly. Also, tiny homes often have unique considerations like weight distribution (especially for mobile units), specialized utility hookups, and ventilation systems tailored to compact living. And let's not forget the importance of understanding local codes – whether it's an ADU on a foundation or a mobile tiny house, the regulatory landscape in San Diego is particular, and our experience navigating it is key to a smooth build. We build homes that are not just small, but also remarkably livable and resilient.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-02"
}